#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0123 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "FLIPPED by the M2-P3 ruling (option (a), Fix #304) - and the corpus's FIRST end-to-end pin of include_empty=true. Row 3's PARAMTYP (the TARGET, not the key) is blank. Before the ruling the D.2 emptiness exception dropped it from both the distinct-value count and the flag pass, leaving {DERIVED} -> counts.size()==1 -> silent, even though PMDA ADaM row 93's second sentence ('If a PARAMCD is said to be derived, all instances must be derived') reads it as a violation. With include_empty=true every blank flavour folds to the single canonical value KeyPart.EMPTY, so group GLUC carries {DERIVED:2, EMPTY:1}, maxCount 2 is held by DERIVED alone, and the minority row 3 is flagged. Exactly one finding: RECORD granularity, no Grouping block. Cross-read with -invalid_blank_paramtyp_tie and -invalid_blank_majority, which pin the two shapes the fixtures did not previously carry. NON-PRECEDENT: the ruling applies to PMDA-AD0123 alone."
#library standard=adamig version=1-0
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 PARAMCD=GLUC
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PARAMCD  type=Char
col PARAMTYP type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC | DERIVED
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | GLUC | DERIVED
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1034 | GLUC |
